    {
      "title": "Overriding Dependencies in Tests",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Overriding Dependencies in Tests",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Override Map",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==app.dependency_overrides[orig] = fake== replaces it for every request",
                "Key is the original **function object**, not a string",
                "Fake's own params resolve as usual: `lambda: User(id=1)` skips auth"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "app.dependency_overrides[get_db] = lambda: test_session",
                "client = TestClient(app)",
                "client.get('/items')  # handler gets test_session"
              ],
              "note": "override first, then call"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What Matches",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "In Depends(...)",
                "Override hits?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Same function object",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`Annotated` alias (wraps same function)",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Imported copy or wrapper",
                  "{red:No}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Reset Every Test",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@pytest.fixture",
                "def client():",
                "    app.dependency_overrides[get_db] = lambda: test_session",
                "    yield TestClient(app)",
                "    app.dependency_overrides.clear()"
              ],
              "note": "teardown after yield clears it"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Leak",
              "text": "No `clear()` means the fake ==leaks into later tests=="
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**What is the override key?** The original function object.",
                "**How to stop leaks?** `clear()` in a yield fixture."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
